.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-PURGE-ALL-QUEUES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-purge-all-queues \- delete all messages from every queue in a region/account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs purge-all-queues
.BR \-\-region | \-r
.I REGION
.BR \-\-accountId | \-a
.I ACCOUNT-ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes all messages from every queue in the given region and account.
No queue is deleted, only its messages. This cannot be undone.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-region " " \fIREGION\fR
Region whose queues should be purged. Required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-accountId " " \fIACCOUNT-ID\fR
Account ID whose queues should be purged. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every matching queue's messages were deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments or the server could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs purge-all-queues \e
    --region eu-central-1 --accountId 000000000000
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-purge-queue (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
